            "key_investigations.1",
            "treatment.0",
            "treatment.1",
            "treatment.2",
            "treatment.3",
            "treatment.4",
            "treatment.5"
          ],
          "text": "On admission, blood glucose was 'HI' on BM, blood ketones 5.2, pH 7.18, bicarbonate 11, and glucose 34. She was managed on the ward HDU with PICU informed. She was treated with the DKA protocol: cautious IV fluids, fixed-rate insulin infusion, potassium replacement, and hourly monitoring. By Day 2, pH had improved to 7.34 and ketones to 0.8. She was subsequently transitioned to subcutaneous insulin on a basal-bolus regimen. Diabetes nurse and dietician input was initiated, with structured education covering carbohydrate counting, hypo management, and sick-day rules. Both the patient and her parents were confident with injections and monitoring prior to discharge on 20/05.",
